IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `types`
IMPORT `chapter-4-exceptions`
IMPORT `chapter-4a-private-defence`

§ `Chapter 14 -- Obscenity`

-- Penal Code 1871 ss 292, 292A, 292B, 293, 294.
-- Source: registers/source-bundle/PC1871.txt.
--
-- The third of three modules for Chapter 14. s 292 is the OBSCENE OBJECT offence in
-- six ways -- dealing, making or possessing for dealing, importing or conveying,
-- profiting from a business, advertising, and offering or attempting -- with two
-- aggravations, electronic dealing to 10 or more individuals (s 292(1A)) and an
-- object depicting a person who is or appears below 18 (s 292(1B)), and one further
-- offence, repeated electronic dealing to 10 or more in total (s 292(1C)). s 292A is
-- the CHILD SEX-DOLL. s 292B is the operator of an ONLINE LOCATION through which
-- obscene objects reach 10 or more. s 293 is dealing to a person BELOW 21. s 294 is
-- the obscene ACT or song in public.
--
-- s 292(2) defines "object" and "obscene object" for ss 292, 292B and 293; the
-- definition is inside the one obscene-object fact. s 292(3) deems an object not
-- obscene where the dealing is authorised by written law, and the Exception takes
-- religious books and temple representations out of ss 292 and 292B. Both are
-- negated conjuncts: s 292(3) on every section that uses the s 292(2) object, the
-- Exception on ss 292 and 292B only.
--
-- ss 292(1A) and (1B) grade punishment and are carried as facts. s 292(1C) is a
-- distinct offence and has its own rule. s 292B(2), the below-18 aggravation of
-- s 292B, shares the (1B) fact.
--
-- PUNISHMENT IS NOT COMPUTED.

§§ `Section 292(2), (3) and the Exception -- What an obscene object is`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 292(2) and (3)"
GIVEN ob IS AN Obscenity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the object is an obscene object within section 292` IF
        ob's `the object is an obscene book pamphlet paper drawing painting representation or figure or any other obscene object including data stored electronically that is capable of conversion to images writing or any other form of representation`
    AND NOT ob's `the sale letting to hire distribution exhibition circulation import export conveyance of or other dealing in the object is authorised by or under written law`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 292 Exception"
GIVEN ob IS AN Obscenity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the religious exception to sections 292 and 292B applies` IF
    ob's `the object is a book pamphlet writing drawing or painting kept or used bona fide for religious purposes or a representation on or in a temple or on a car used for the conveyance of idols or kept or used for a religious purpose`

§§ `Section 292 -- Sale of obscene objects`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 292(1)"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes sale, distribution, making, importing or advertising of an obscene object under Penal Code 1871 section 292
GIVEN ob IS AN Obscenity @desc Selling, hiring out, distributing, exhibiting or circulating an obscene object; making or possessing one for that purpose; importing or conveying one for it or knowing it will be so dealt with; profiting from a business that so deals; advertising such dealing; or offering or attempting any of these. Not where the dealing is authorised by written law or the object is religious.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes an obscene object offence` IF
        `the object is an obscene object within section 292` ob
    AND NOT `the religious exception to sections 292 and 292B applies` ob
    AND (   ob's `sells lets to hire distributes publicly exhibits or puts into circulation the obscene object by any means electronic or otherwise`
         OR ob's `makes produces or has in his possession the obscene object for the purposes of sale hire distribution public exhibition or circulation by any means electronic or otherwise`
         OR ob's `imports exports or conveys the obscene object for the purposes of sale hire distribution public exhibition or circulation or knowing or having reason to believe that it will be sold let to hire distributed publicly exhibited or put into circulation by any means electronic or otherwise`
         OR ob's `takes part in or receives profits from a business in the course of which he knows or has reason to believe that an obscene object is made produced purchased kept imported exported or conveyed for the purposes of sale hire distribution public exhibition or circulation or is sold let to hire distributed publicly exhibited or put into circulation by any means electronic or otherwise`
         OR ob's `advertises or makes known by any means whatsoever that any person is engaged or is ready to engage in an act which is an offence under section 292 or that an obscene object can be procured from or through any person`
         OR ob's `offers or attempts to do an act which is an offence under section 292`)

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 292(1A) and (1B)"
GIVEN ob IS AN Obscenity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the obscene object offence is aggravated by electronic reach or a minor depicted` IF
        `constitutes an obscene object offence` ob
    AND (   ob's `the dealing is by electronic means to 10 or more individuals`
         OR ob's `the obscene object depicts an image of a person who is or who appears to a reasonable observer to be or is implied to be below 18 years of age`)

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 292(1C)"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes repeated electronic distribution of obscene objects to 10 or more individuals under Penal Code 1871 section 292(1C)
GIVEN ob IS AN Obscenity @desc On 2 or more occasions selling, hiring out, distributing, exhibiting or circulating an obscene object by electronic means to a total of 10 or more individuals.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes repeated electronic distribution of obscene objects` IF
        `the object is an obscene object within section 292` ob
    AND NOT `the religious exception to sections 292 and 292B applies` ob
    AND ob's `on 2 or more occasions sells lets to hire distributes publicly exhibits or puts into circulation by electronic means an obscene object to a total number of 10 or more individuals`

§§ `Section 292A -- Child sex-doll`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 292A"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes possession, distribution or making of a child sex-doll under Penal Code 1871 section 292A
GIVEN ob IS AN Obscenity @desc Importing, exporting, conveying, selling, hiring out, distributing, circulating, making, producing or possessing an anatomically correct doll, mannequin or robot with the features of, or appearing to resemble, a person below 16 and intended for sexual use.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes a child sex-doll offence` IF
    ob's `imports exports conveys sells lets to hire distributes puts into circulation makes produces or is in possession of an anatomically correct doll mannequin or robot with the features of or with features that appear to a reasonable observer to resemble a person below 16 years of age and intended for use in sexual activities`

§§ `Section 292B -- Obscene object on an online location`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 292B"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes operating an online location through which obscene objects are distributed to 10 or more individuals under Penal Code 1871 section 292B
GIVEN ob IS AN Obscenity @desc An obscene object reaching 10 or more individuals on an online location, the person developing, maintaining, managing, regulating access to or exercising editorial control over that location, intending it to be used to enable or facilitate the dealing in obscene objects generally.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes operating an online location for obscene objects` IF
        `the object is an obscene object within section 292` ob
    AND NOT `the religious exception to sections 292 and 292B applies` ob
    AND ob's `an obscene object is sold let for hire distributed publicly exhibited or circulated to 10 or more individuals on an online location being an internet domain website webpage chatroom channel group forum or other location accessible by means of the Internet`
    AND ob's `develops and maintains the online location or organises manages or supervises its use or manages or regulates membership of or access to it or has the authority to decide whether material may be included or excluded on it or where to place material or otherwise exercises editorial control over it`
    AND ob's `in doing so intends that the online location be used to enable or facilitate the sale hire distribution public exhibition or circulation of obscene objects generally`

§§ `Sections 293 and 294 -- Young persons, and obscene acts`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 293"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes sale or distribution of an obscene object to a young person under Penal Code 1871 section 293
GIVEN ob IS AN Obscenity @desc Selling, hiring out, distributing, exhibiting or circulating a s 292(2) obscene object to a person below 21, or offering or attempting to.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes dealing in an obscene object to a young person` IF
        `the object is an obscene object within section 292` ob
    AND ob's `sells lets to hire distributes exhibits or circulates the obscene object to a person below 21 years of age or offers or attempts to do so`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 294"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes an obscene act or song in a public place under Penal Code 1871 section 294
GIVEN ob IS AN Obscenity @desc To the annoyance of others, doing an obscene act in a public place, or singing, reciting or uttering obscene words in or near one.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes an obscene act in public` IF
    ob's `to the annoyance of others does an obscene act in a public place or sings recites or utters obscene words in or near a public place`

§§ `Proposed Act wrappers`

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes an obscenity offence` IF
        (   `constitutes an obscene object offence` (a's `obscenity`)
         OR `constitutes repeated electronic distribution of obscene objects` (a's `obscenity`)
         OR `constitutes a child sex-doll offence` (a's `obscenity`)
         OR `constitutes operating an online location for obscene objects` (a's `obscenity`)
         OR `constitutes dealing in an obscene object to a young person` (a's `obscenity`)
         OR `constitutes an obscene act in public` (a's `obscenity`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)
